# TwinCAT MCP Build Automation

## Tool discovery (canonical)

Use **`GetMcpTools(server, toolName)`** before each call. Do not discover
schemas by reading `mcps/**/tools/*.json`. Server IDs: see
`twincat3-mcp-runtime` (team plugin vs local `user-mcp-twincat-local`).

## Available MCP Tools

### Requires TcXaeShell (XAE)

| Tool | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| `twincat_status` | XAE install/running, `instances[]`, MCP session, `prereqs`, dialogs |
| `twincat_open` | Open / attach; returns `pin_honored` / `attached_xae_version` |
| `twincat_check_all_objects` | Compile ALL objects — includes `errors[]`, `warnings[]`, `infos[]` |
| `twincat_build` | Incremental build (`full_rebuild=true` for RebuildSolution) |
| `twincat_get_output_log` | Re-read build pane only — not needed after check/build |
| `twincat_reload` | Close+reopen solution — **only** after `.plcproj` was changed |
| `twincat_export_library` | Export library; default `wait=false`; `wait=true`+`timeout_seconds>90` coerced to async. Echoes paths/version. |
| `twincat_export_progress` | Live export poll (`running`, `phase`, `percent`, final `result{}`) |
| `twincat_export_check_artifacts` | Disk-only verify after `-32001` / unclear finish — if `all_present` do **not** re-export |
| `twincat_dismiss_safe_dialogs` | Dismiss idle “file changed outside” reload prompts (Yes/Ja) |
| `twincat_close` | Release MCP session (quit only if MCP started XAE; else detach) |
| `twincat_stweep_status` | STweep install + Formatcode commands (+ format_progress snapshot) |
| `twincat_format_code` | STweep Format code (default `wait=false`; project needs `confirm`) |
| `twincat_format_progress` | Live format job poll while formatting |
| `twincat_format_cancel` | Abort multi-file format between files (`phase=canceled`) |

STweep details: rule `twincat3-mcp-stweep` / skill `twincat3-stweep-format`.

### Export scope: release / new-version vs online-test

| Context | `.library` | `.compiled-library` |
|---------|------------|---------------------|
| **Ship gate / release** (`/twincat3-cmd-new-version`, `/twincat3-cmd-release`; skills `twincat3-new-version`, `twincat3-release`) | **required** | **required** |
| **Online / UmRT live diagnose** (`/twincat3-cmd-online-test`, skill `twincat3-umrt-systemtest`) | required (if export needed) | **skip** (`compiled_library=false`) — time saver only |

Never skip `.compiled-library` on a ship gate / release just to save time.

### No XAE needed

| Tool | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| `twincat_plcproj_info` | Read version/title from `.plcproj` |
| `twincat_plcproj_verify` / `twincat_plcproj_sync` | plcproj ↔ disk |
| `twincat_migrate` / `twincat_fup_migrate` / `twincat_cfc_migrate` | FBD/CFC → ST |
| `twincat_infosys_mshc_search` / `_read` | Offline InfoSys |

## Validation (short)

1. `twincat_open(path="<.sln preferred | .plcproj | folder>")`
2. `twincat_check_all_objects`
3. Fix → repeat step 2

Detailed workflow: skill `twincat3-validate`.

## Critical Rules for `twincat_open`

- Prefer **`.sln`** when known (best multi-instance attach). `.plcproj` / folder also work.
- Multi-PLC solutions: tool returns the project list — pass the exact `.plcproj`.
- **ROT attach:** finds the running XAE that already has this solution (TE1000 pattern). Does not start a duplicate only because another window is active.
- **`xae_version`** (optional): `"4024"`/`"15.0"` or `"4026"`/`"17.0"`. Use only when the user asks or a specific shell is required.
  - Empty: attach to matching open solution; if creating new, prefer an already-running shell version, else newest registered.
  - If the solution is **already open** in another shell version, attach to that instance (no duplicate) even when `xae_version` differs.
- Check response: `success`, `created_new_instance`, `xae_version`, `attached_xae_version`, `pin_honored`, `pin_ignored_reason`, `xae_prog_id`, `solution_path`. Unexpected `created_new_instance=true` when the project was already open → report, do not ignore.
- Content edits (`.TcPOU`/`.TcDUT`/`.TcGVL`): **no** reload. Reload **only** if `.plcproj` changed: `twincat_open` (if needed) → `twincat_reload` → check.
- Libraries → `twincat_check_all_objects`. Apps/boot → `twincat_build`.

## Session / XAE dialog playbook (mandatory)

Disk edits (comment/format/git) while POUs are open → sequential “file has been
changed outside … Reload?” prompts. They **can** block COM. Do **not** invent
manual clicking.

```text
WHEN COM fails / open-build-format-export stalls / you suspect XAE popups:

1) twincat_status
2) READ: blocking_dialogs[], instances[].dte_busy, dismissed_dialogs_recent
3) IF any blocking_dialogs with auto_dismissable=true
      → call twincat_dismiss_safe_dialogs ONCE
      → twincat_status again
      → IF cleared → RETRY the original MCP call once
4) IF blocking_dialogs remain with auto_dismissable=false
      → STOP. Tell user the dialog title/text. Do NOT invent clicks.
5) IF blocking_dialogs empty but dte_busy=true
      → wait briefly, status again; do not spam COM
6) NEVER say "I will close the XAE dialogs manually" as the plan
7) NEVER assume N dialogs for one FB name = N parallel windows
   (XAE shows them sequentially; dismiss tool clears the queue)
```

| DO | DON'T |
|----|--------|
| `twincat_status` first | Blind-retry COM until timeout |
| `twincat_dismiss_safe_dialogs` for known reload prompts | Narrate manual clicking in XAE |
| Retry original tool **once** after clear | Re-export / re-format while dialogs up |
| Ask user only if not auto-dismissable | Claim “N dialogs for FB X” without status evidence |

## Export recovery after Cursor `-32001`

`-32001` is a **client idle timeout**, not proof that XAE failed.

1. `twincat_export_progress` — if `running=true` → keep polling (do **not** re-export)
2. If `running=false` and `result.success` → done
3. Else `twincat_export_check_artifacts` — if `all_present` → success (no re-export)
4. Only if artifacts missing → one retry with `wait=false`

## Session lifecycle

Do **not** call `twincat_close` unless XAE is unresponsive or the user asks. Keep the session open; the next `twincat_open` re-attaches via ROT by solution path. Optional `force_quit=true` terminates XAE even when MCP only attached — use with caution.
